## 1. Threat Model & Goals

### What "Deletion Vault" Guarantees

| Guarantee | Mechanism |
|-----------|-----------|
| Every file delete is intercepted | Minifilter altitude 360000 — above NTFS, below antivirus |
| File content is preserved before destruction | Pre-operation copy in kernel context |
| Works against ALL processes including SYSTEM / admin | Minifilter operates in ring-0, no userland bypass |
| Vault cannot be deleted by the same process | Self-protection via FltDeleteFile refusal on vault path |
| Evidence chain is intact (SHA-256, timestamps) | Hash computed pre-copy, sealed in metadata.json |

### Attack Surfaces NOT Covered
- Raw disk writes (bypassing NTFS entirely — e.g., `\\.\PhysicalDrive0`)
- Kernel-mode rootkits with altitude above yours
- Secure-erase tools that zero in-place before delete (content lost before IRP fires)
- Memory-mapped files deleted via `NtSetInformationFile` while still mapped (handled — see §3.5)

