## 7. Encryption & Integrity

### 7.1 Per-File Encryption

```cpp
// crypto_engine.cpp

#include <bcrypt.h>
#pragma comment(lib, "bcrypt.lib")

void CryptoEngine::EncryptFile(const std::wstring& vaultPath)
{
    // Key: 256-bit master key (DPAPI-protected at rest)
    // Nonce: 96-bit cryptographically random per file
    // Tag: 128-bit GCM authentication tag (appended to ciphertext)

    BYTE nonce[12], tag[16], key[32];
    LoadMasterKey(key);          // Unwrap from DPAPI/TPM store
    BCryptGenRandom(nullptr, nonce, 12, BCRYPT_USE_SYSTEM_PREFERRED_RNG);

    // Open vault file, read plaintext, encrypt in 256KB chunks
    // Write format: [12-byte nonce][ciphertext][16-byte GCM tag]
    // Original plaintext file is zeroed and replaced with ciphertext

    EncryptFileAesGcm(vaultPath, key, nonce, tag);

    // Store nonce in metadata JSON (tag as well for verification)
    SecureZeroMemory(key, 32);
}
```

### 7.2 Master Key Storage Strategy

| Option | Mechanism | Threat Resistance |
|--------|-----------|-------------------|
| **TPM 2.0 sealed** | Key sealed to PCR state (boot chain) | High — key unusable if BIOS modified |
| **DPAPI LocalMachine** | `CryptProtectData(CRYPTPROTECT_LOCAL_MACHINE)` | Medium — admin can decrypt |
| **Smart card** | PKCS#11 / PIV | Highest — requires physical token |
| **Passphrase** | Argon2id KDF → AES-256 | Low-Medium — PIN required at startup |

**Recommended:** TPM 2.0 sealed + PIN stretch via Argon2id as backup unlock.

